If You're Targeting Product-Based Companies

A strong array foundation should include:

✅ Array traversal
✅ Searching
✅ Sorting
✅ Two pointers
✅ Sliding window
✅ Prefix sum
✅ Hashing
✅ Kadane's algorithm
✅ Matrix operations
✅ Binary search
✅ Greedy techniques

Mastering these patterns will prepare you for the majority of array questions asked in interviews at companies like Amazon, Microsoft, Google, Adobe, Atlassian, Walmart Global Tech, and many others.

Tip: For each problem you solve, don't just memorize the code. Ask yourself:

What pattern does this use?
What's the time complexity?
What's the space complexity?
Can I solve it in a more optimal way?

Recognizing patterns is what makes new interview problems much easier to solve.